* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
# systemd parses unit files literally: a CRLF here makes values like
# SuccessExitStatus=10 arrive with a trailing CR and fail to parse. These get
# scp'd to the Linux hosts straight from the repo, so pin them the way *.sh is.
# (This comment used to embed a literal CR to illustrate that. Don't put it
# back: a whole-file CRLF->LF conversion turns it into a real line break, which
# splits the comment and leaves git parsing the tail as an attribute name.)
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf

# Dockerfiles and the SQL/requirements files beside them are scp'd to the Linux
# host and built there. A CRLF in a Dockerfile breaks line continuations, and
# pip has choked on CR-terminated requirement lines. Pin them the way *.sh is.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
requirements.txt text eol=lf
